<Layout title="Blavet" description="Michel Blavet’s flute Sonata II “La Vibray”, Op. 2 No. 2: form, cadences, partimento patterns and how to play the flute part, movement by movement.">
  <main class="page-block wide">
    <h1>Blavet</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Michel Blavet (1700–1768) was the leading French flautist of his day. His Sonata II, “La Vibray”, from the
      <em>Sonates mêlées de pièces</em>, Op. 2 (Paris, 1731), is read here movement by movement: its form, its cadences, the
      partimento patterns under the melody, and the flute part as Quantz’s rules would have it played.
    </p>
    <PageList pages={BLAVET} />
    <p class="source-note">Each page lists its own sources and the sound samples it uses.</p>
  </main>
</Layout>
